[0.935245, "o", "H wheel ownership\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\u001b[2;55H  \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;5;252mrailmux ssh — agent-pane wheel served locally, not forwarded upstream:\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[3;55H  1. handle_terminal_part gets the SgrMouseEvent and dispatches to LocalHistoryView.wheel.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[4;55H  2. wheel() resolves the pane via _route_at; a hit on an agent viewport scrolls _HistoryViewport.offset and returns HistoryAc\u001b[5;55Htion with render_history=True and forwarded_input=b\"\"\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[6;55H  — no upstream input.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[7;55H  3. apply_history_action only sends upstream when action.forwarded_input is set; empty means nothing reaches tmux. The overla\u001b[8;55Hy is painted client-side via surface.paint_overlays.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[9;55H  4. This is a fast-client history overlay over bounded snapshots, not tmux copy-mode; the implementation notes stock tmux Whe\u001b[10;55HelUpPane would enter copy-mode, which is deliberately\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[11;55H  avoided.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[12;55H  Focused test: tests/test_fast_full_window.py::test_local_history_routes_sidebar_immediately_and_owns_agent_wheel asserts age\u001b[13;55Hnt_action.forwarded_input == b\"\".\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[14;55H  Suggested addition: assert agent_action.render_history is True, proving the overlay rendered rather than merely dropping the\u001b[15;55H event.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[16;55H\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;239m\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[33;55H─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;147m\u001b[34;55H❯\u001b[39m \u001b[K\u001b[38;5;239m\u001b[35;55H──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[0.935865, "o", "────────\u001b[36;55H─────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;244m\u001b[37;55H  ⏵⏵ normal mode · shift+tab to cycle · ← for agents\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[30m\u001b[48;5;70m\r\n Railmux · Claude Code                                                                                       \u001b[38;5;231mProject: /demo/railmux-web-workspace-v1/projects/railmux  (3 sessions)\u001b[30m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1;1H\u001b[1;37r\u001b[1;55H\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\u001b[1d\u001b[38;5;252m ▐▛███▜▌   Claude Code v2.1.220\u001b[2;55H▝▜█████▛▘  Opus 5 (1M context) · API Usage Billing\u001b[3;55H  ▘▘ ▝▝    /demo/railmux-web-workspace-v1/projects/railmux\u001b[5;55H\u001b[38;5;147m❯\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252mIn railmux ssh, explain how a mouse-wheel event over an agent pane is served from the fast client's local history overlay\u001b[6;55H  rather than forwarded upstream. Point to the exact implementation symbols and one existing focused test that directly\u001b[7;55H  asserts empty forwarded_input. Then suggest one small additional assertion.\u001b[9;55H\u001b[38;5;147m●\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1mTrace SSH wheel ownership\u001b[10;55H  \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;5;252mrailmux ssh — agent-pane wheel served locally, not forwarded upstream:\u001b[11;55H  1. handle_terminal_part gets the SgrMouseEvent and dispatches to LocalHistoryView.wheel.\u001b[12;55H  2. wheel() resolves the pane via _route_at; a hit on an agent viewport scrolls _HistoryViewport.offset and returns\u001b[13;55H  HistoryAction with render_history=True and forwarded_input=b\"\" — no upstream input.\u001b[14;55H  3. apply_history_action only sends upstream when action.forwarded_input is set; empty means nothing reaches tmux. The\u001b[15;55H  overlay is painted client-side via surface.paint_overlays.\u001b[16;55H  4. This is a fast-client history overlay over bounded snapshots, not tmux copy-mode; the implementation notes stock tmux\u001b[17;55H  WheelUpPane would enter copy-mode, which is deliberately avoided.\u001b[18;55H  Focused test: tests/test_fast_full_window.py::test_local_history_routes_sidebar_immediately_and_owns_agent_wheel asserts\u001b[19;55H  agent_action.forwarded_input == b\"\".\u001b[20;55H  Suggested addition: assert agent_action.render_history is True, proving the overlay rendered rather than merely dropping\u001b[21;55H  the event.\u001b[34;55H\u001b[38;5;239m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[35;55H"]
