r_history=True and forwarded_input=b\"\" — no upstream input.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[14;55H  3. apply_history_action only sends upstream when action.forwarded_input is set; empty means nothing reaches tmux. The\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[15;55H  overlay is painted client-side via surface.paint_overlays.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[16;55H  4. This is a fast-client history overlay over bounded snapshots, not tmux copy-mode; the implementation notes stock tmux\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[17;55H  WheelUpPane would enter copy-mode, which is deliberately avoided.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[18;55H  Focused test: tests/test_fast_full_window.py::test_local_history_routes_sidebar_immediately_and_owns_agent_wheel asserts\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[19;55H  agent_action.forwarded_input == b\"\".\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[20;55H  Suggested addition: assert agent_action.render_history is True, proving the overlay rendered rather than merely dropping\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[21;55H  the event.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[22;55H\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;239m\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;147m\u001b[35;55H❯\u001b[39m \u001b[K\u001b[38;5;239m\u001b[36;55H───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
