;252mrailmux ssh — agent-pane wheel served locally, not forwarded upstream:\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[11;55H  1. handle_terminal_part gets the SgrMouseEvent and dispatches to LocalHistoryView.wheel.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[12;55H  2. wheel() resolves the pane via _route_at; a hit on an agent viewport scrolls _HistoryViewport.offset and returns\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[13;55H  HistoryAction with render_history=True and forwarded_input=b\"\" — no upstream input.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[14;55H  3. apply_history_action only sends upstream when action.forwarded_input is set; empty means nothing reaches tmux. The\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[15;55H  overlay is painted client-side via surface.paint_overlays.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[16;55H  4. This is a fast-client history overlay over bounded snapshots, not tmux copy-mode; the implementation notes stock tmux\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[17;55H  WheelUpPane would enter copy-mode, which is deliberately avoided.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[18;55H  Focused test: tests/test_fast_full_window.py::test_local_history_routes_sidebar_immediately_and_owns_agent_wheel asserts\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[19;55H  agent_action.forwarded_input == b\"\".\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[20;55H  Suggested addition: assert agent_action.render_history is True, proving the overlay rendered rather than merely dropping\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[21;55H  the event.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[22;55H\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;239m\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;147m\u001b[35;55H❯\u001b[39m \u001b[K\u001b[38;5;239m\u001b[36;55H───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[5.068928, "o", "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;244m\u001b[37;55H  ⏵⏵ normal mode · shift+tab to cycle · ← for agents\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[30m\u001b[48;5;70m\r\n Railmux · Codex · ▣                                                                                         \u001b[38;5;231mProject: /demo/railmux-web-workspace-v1/projects/railmux  (1 sessions)\u001b[30m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[37;27H\u001b[H\u001b[38;5;70m\u001b[1m─ PROJECTS ───────────────────────────────────── 1 ─\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1X\u001b[4;1H\u001b[38;5;231m\u001b[48;5;22m\u001b[1m  railmux                                         1 \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1X\r\n\u001b[38;5;252m                                                    \u001b[39m\u001b[1X\r\n\u001b[38;5;252m                                                    \u001b[39m\u001b[1X\u001b[9;1H\u001b[38;5;70m\u001b[1m─ \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;5;244mSESSIONS (railmux)\u001b[38;5;70m\u001b[1m ───────────────────────────\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;5;244m 1 \u001b[38;5;70m\u001b[1m─\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[1X\u001b[12;1H\u001b[38;5;244m◦\u001b[38;5;252m Explain workspace layout                          \u001b[39m\u001b[1X\u001b[14;1H\u001b[38;5;252m               "]
