H\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;147m\n❯\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252mIn railmux ssh, explain how a mouse-wheel event over an agent pane is served from the fast client's local history overlay\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[6;38H  rather than forwarded upstream. Point to the exact implementation symbols and one existing focused test that directly\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[7;38H  asserts empty forwarded_input. Then suggest one small additional assertion.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[8;38H\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;147m\n●\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252m"]
[6.550009, "o", "\u001b[1mTrace SSH wheel ownership\u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1m\u001b[10;38H  \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;5;252mrailmux ssh — agent-pane wheel served locally, not forwarded upstream:\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[11;38H  1. handle_terminal_part gets the SgrMouseEvent and dispatches to LocalHistoryView.wheel.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[12;38H  2. wheel() resolves the pane via _route_at; a hit on an agent viewport scrolls _HistoryViewport.offset and returns\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[13;38H  HistoryAction with render_history=True and forwarded_input=b\"\" — no upstream input.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[14;38H  3. apply_history_action only sends upstream when action.forwarded_input is set; empty means nothing reaches tmux. The\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[15;38H  overlay is painted client-side via surface.paint_overlays.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[16;38H  4. This is a fast-client history overlay over bounded snapshots, not tmux copy-mode; the implementation notes stock tmux\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[17;38H  WheelUpPane would enter copy-mode, which is deliberately avoided.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[18;38H  Focused test: tests/test_fast_full_window.py::test_local_history_routes_sidebar_immediately_and_owns_agent_wheel asserts\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[19;38H  agent_action.forwarded_input == b\"\".\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[20;38H  Suggested addition: assert agent_action.render_history is True, proving the overlay rendered rather than merely dropping\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[21;38H  the event.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[22;38H\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;239m\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;147m\u001b[35;38H❯\u001b[39m \u001b[K\u001b[38;5;239m\u001b[36;38H───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[6.550418, "o", "──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;244m\u001b[37;38H  ⏵⏵ normal mode · shift+tab to cycle · ← for agents\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[30m\u001b[48;5;70m\r\n Railmux · Codex · ▣                                                                                         \u001b[38;5;231mProject: /demo/railmux-web-workspace-v1/projects/railmux  (1 sessions)\u001b[30m \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[27;53H\u001b[1;37r\u001b[1;38H\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\n\u001b[K\u001b[1d\u001b[38;5;252m ▐▛███▜▌   Claude Code v2.1.220\u001b[2;38H▝▜█████▛▘  Opus 5 (1M context) · API Usage Billing\u001b[3;38H  ▘▘ ▝▝    /demo/railmux-web-workspace-v1/projects/railmux\u001b[5;38H\u001b[38;5;147m❯\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252mIn railmux ssh, explain how a mouse-wheel event over an agent pane is served from the fast client's local history overlay rather than\u001b[6;38H  forwarded upstream. Point to the exact implementation symbols and one existing focused test that directly asserts empty forwarded_input.\u001b[7;38H  Then suggest one small additional assertion.\u001b[9;38H\u001b[38;5;147m●\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;252m\u001b[1mTrace SSH wheel ownership\u001b[10;38H  \u001b(B\u001b[m\u001b[38;5;252mrailmux ssh — agent-pane wheel served locally, not forwarded upstream:\u001b[11;38H  1. handle_terminal_part gets the SgrMouseEvent and dispatches to LocalHistoryView.wheel.\u001b[12;38H  2. wheel() resolves the pane via _route_at; a hit on an agent viewport scrolls _HistoryViewport.offset and returns HistoryAction with\u001b[13;38H  render_history=True and forwarded_input=b\"\" — no upstream input.\u001b[14;38H  3. apply_history_action only sends upstream when action.forwarded_input is set; empty means nothing reaches tmux. The overlay is painted\u001b[15;38H  client-side via surface.paint_overlays.\u001b[16;38H  4. This is a fast-client history overlay over bounded snapshots, not tmux copy-mode; the implementation notes stock tmux WheelUpPane would\u001b[17;38H  enter copy-mode, which is deliberately avoided.\u001b[18;38H  Focused test: tests/test_fast_full_window.py::test_local_history_routes_sidebar_immediately_and_owns_agent_wheel asserts\u001b[19;38H  agent_action.forwarded_input == b\"\".\u001b[20;38H  Suggested addition: assert agent_action.render_history is True, proving the overlay rendered rather than merely dropping the event.\u001b[34;38H\u001b[38;5;239m──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[35;38H\u001b[38;5;147m❯\u001b[39m \u001b[36;38H\u001b[38;5;239m────"]
